/**
 * The wrought-iron "H" crest, as PDF-embeddable bytes.
 *
 * WHY A BASE64 CONSTANT AND NOT AN IMPORT
 * ---------------------------------------
 * `workRecordDocument.ts` is deliberately free of React, Capacitor and `@/`
 * aliases so the exact bytes of the shared record can be generated and
 * inspected outside a browser. It also has to work OFFLINE inside a
 * WKWebView — the PDF is built on demand, on a phone, in a leasing office —
 * so fetching the mark at generation time would add a network failure path to
 * a function that currently has none, and a work record that renders without
 * its own logo because the wifi dropped is worse than one that never had it.
 *
 * WHY PNG AND NOT THE APP'S WEBP
 * ------------------------------
 * `src/assets/helpr-logo-{96,256}.webp` are what the React tree renders.
 * jsPDF cannot decode WEBP at all — it accepts PNG, JPEG and a couple of raw
 * formats — so the source here is `public/helpr-splash-icon.png`, the same
 * crest, downscaled from 512x440 to 128x110 (oxipng -o max, alpha preserved)
 * because it is drawn at roughly 26pt. That is ~305dpi at print size and
 * ~32KB of base64, in a module only reached from the dynamic
 * `buildWorkRecordPdf` import, so /work-record does not pay for it on load.
 *
 * If the crest ever changes, regenerate from the same source:
 *   sips -Z 128 --out /tmp/h.png public/helpr-splash-icon.png
 *   oxipng -o max --strip all /tmp/h.png && base64 -i /tmp/h.png
 */

